5 gismu and a cmavo rafsi does wind up with a huge lujvo, though, but then I
think a lot of precision is needed in this general vein, because there are a
lot of subtly different viewpoints. "God can be disproven but not proven",
"God can be proven but not disproven", "God can be either proven or
disproven", "God can be neither disproven nor disproven". And all of those
are in some sense the English word "agnostic" if you throw in "and I don't
have a belief as to what the answer is", even though they're obviously
entirely different. (Although admittedly the latter has the term "strong
agnostic" tied to it in English, but still.)

